Yesterday I was playing a few wizards, and was thinking about what the
best possible start-up inventory could be. Heres what I would go for
if I could control the RNG (assuming a magic marker and blind fold as
well):

Blessed scrolls of charging, enchant armour, and genocide. EA can be
read right off the bat for a small AC boost, charging can be used when
the marker runs low, and genocide can be used either in a pant-
shitting emergency or to wipe out your least favourtie species (if you
run into trouble in the mines, you might do both with by genociding
h!). Also, having knowledge of these scrolls is also handy for magic
marker writing as well.

For potions, I'd take 2 blessed gain abilities and 1 holy water. The
boosts to Str and Con mean a handy extra 100 carry capacity, and will
probably ensure hungerless casting if you were unfortunate to start
with 16 or less Int. Starting with Holy water has obvious benefits
too, you can start manufacturing more as soon as you grab a pick-axe,
a few junk potions, and find a fountain. You could also start writing
blessed enchant armours very early too.

I'd take a spellbook of Identify, just because it is so damn useful,
and the earlier you can cast it the better, although you may need a
level 1/2 Divination spell to build it up first. That can be arranged
as soon as you max your luck though.

For rings, there are quite a lot of goods ones to choose from. I'd
probably settle for Teleport Control (convience + emergency, once you
find a nymph or too) and Free Action.

Finally, a wand of death, for getting you out of almost any fight that
has turned bad. A wand of cancellation might be handy too, mainly so
you have knowledge of it (help prevent accidents), and lets you create
holy water/blank scrolls as soon as you find the junk to blank.

So, what would you choose?



